NAME: a repeat whose JMP moves a pointer
DESCRIPTION: (repeat body (Inc p)): the JMP's B operand increments p every iteration, so no jump may be threaded past that JMP; see behtests/repeat_data_moves_pointer.beh
SRC:
(let (x 0)
  (let (p 0)
    (let (k 3)
      (seq
        (repeat
          (seq (if (JZ k) (JMP 0)) (SUB 1 k) (if (JN x) (NOP)))
          (Inc p))
        (DAT (store x) (store p))
        (DAT (store k) 0)))))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b

_REP6 
  JMN.A  $_IF9  , $_LET3 
  JMP    #0     , #0     
_IF9  
  SUB.A  #1     , $_LET3 
  JMZ.A  $_IF14 , $_LET1 
  NOP    #0     , #0     
_IF14 
  JMP    $_REP6 , >_LET2 
_LET1 
_LET2 
  DAT    #0     , #0     
_LET3 
  DAT    #3     , #0     
  DAT    $0     , $0     